The Emperor Has No Clothes

**(Because you work with CHARITABLE ORGANIZATIONS)**

VISIT HERE OR PRESS THE PHOTO BELOW FOR ARTICLE https://jimmylarose.acemlnd.com/lt.php?x=3DZy~GDJJFjP6pSqyA~IUeCe2nQljgLuk-cvjKHFVnCb6s4s-ky.0eFr23FziNT3jNYxY5gWJXKZ62

https://jimmylarose.acemlnd.com/lt.php?x=3DZy~GDJJFjP6pSqyA~IUeCe2nQljgLuk-cvjKHFVnCb6s4s-ky.0eFr23FziNT3jNYxY5gWJXKZ62 

Dear Colleague In Service,

**Major Gifts Ramp-Up Controversy - The Emperor Has No Clothes** takes a look at charity's brokenness and the solutions nonprofits must deploy to end the crazy-making. Major Gifts Ramp-Up (MGRU) is not nonprofit management 101. Rather, it is for seasoned c-suite executives who dare to confront this train wreck we call charity. It is a tightly facilitated 2-day session that uses an "emperor has no clothes" approach that celebrates participants' convictions. MGRU relies on the audience to inspire confidence and change. Simply put, a Major Gifts Ramp-Up Event 

**will challenge everything you believe about nonprofit management and the raising of money.**

**"Major Gifts Ramp-Up is for seasoned c-suite executives who possess the courage to confront this train wreck we call charity!"**

Did you know, that charity spends over 1.2 trillion dollars annually (U.S. Chamber of Commerce). YES, not billions, but 1.2 TRILLION!

CHARITY IS BEREFT OF GREAT LEADERS. The nonprofit sector is larger than U.S. manufacturing and yet our boards and executives oversee the mismanagement of trillions at the expense of men, women, children and families in need. Someone has to say it, someone has to point and shout "THE EMPEROR HAS NO CLOTHES".

How? Let's start by coming together for Major Gifts Ramp-Up...VISIT HERE TO READ ENTIRE ARTICLE https://jimmylarose.acemlnd.com/lt.php?x=3DZy~GDJJFjP6pSqyA~IUeCe2nQljgLuk-cvjKHFVnCb6s4s-ky.0eFr23FziNT3jNYxY5gWJXKZ62

Inside Charity is pleased to report that over 500,000 executives, staff, board members, ministry leaders and volunteers rely on Inside Charity for their nonprofit news. We're grateful to everyone who has participated and want to encourage as many as people as possible to continue to share their experiences. Your written comments and contributions have helped your colleagues navigate this process.

Inside Charity is here to make sure receive the information you require to navigate unprecedented times.

VISIT HERE TO SUBSCRIBE https://jimmylarose.acemlnd.com/lt.php?x=3DZy~GDJJFjP6pSqyA~IUeCe2nQljgLuk-cvjKHFVnCb6s4s-ky.0eFr23FziNT3jNYxY5gWJXKZ62

We look forward to hearing from you.

Warmly,

**Kathleen Robinson, Ph.D.**

Senior Editor

